{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunobi-ninja/kache/pulls/1493","id":4811853609,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRBv5c8AAAABHs8PKQ","html_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1493","diff_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1493.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1493.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunobi-ninja/kache/issues/1493","number":1493,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf(predictions): cut the tree guard's cost per workspace crate","user":{"login":"jleni","id":13698520,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjk4NTIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13698520?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni","html_url":"https://github.com/jleni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The perf gate on #1491 flagged aube warm builds under contention as 8.5% slower (25.6 s to 28.2 s, paired test), and the regression is on main now. All of it comes from the predictions tree guard #1491 added, which checks every workspace crate's record against a digest of its tree.\n\nOn a warm aube build in the same path, the guard added about 2 s of key time per build:\n\n- About 1.3 s: crates with a build script never hit the digest memo. It was filed under the whole root set, including the crate's own OUT_DIR, whose inode and times are new in every fresh target dir. Each such crate read about 1,300 workspace files again, none of them big enough to keep a hash row.\n- About 0.9 s: each of 24 workspace crates stat-walked the 1,690-entry workspace on every key.\n\nRegistry crates and build-script declared inputs did not change (9 ms per build).\n\n## What changes\n\n- Each root of a tree digest is memoised on its own, so every crate shares the workspace digest and a crate with an OUT_DIR folds only that directory. Several roots combine under a labelled digest; a single root keeps today's digest.\n- A tree memo is found by the stamp of its entries, without the root directory's own times, so creating `target/` or running `cargo clean` no longer invalidates it.\n- A build-script compile's guard leaves out the profile's target directory, as every other unit's does.\n- The walk stats each entry through the directory that listed it.\n\nEvery change keeps what the guard notices: an entry added, removed, renamed or rewritten anywhere in a guarded tree still changes the digest.\n\nDo not merge yet: an adversarial review with a second model and an A/B measurement are still running, and the contention batches may need concurrent walks of one workspace coalesced. This PR is open now so the perf gate can measure it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, the cache_key, tree_stamp, build_script and wrapper unit tests (884), and input_prediction_test, build_script_declared_inputs_test and cached_units_regression_test pass on macOS.\n- Measured locally on aube, warm in the same path: workspace key time per build 3.7 s on #1491's head, 2.0 s with these changes, 1.5-1.7 s on the merge base before #1491.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:19:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T14:57:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T14:57:22Z","merged_at":"2026-10-10T14:57:22Z","merge_commit_sha":"7af7c714bd42dc064753485bab8d28194058135d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.gi